  "story": [
    "Théo runs the final <span class=\"hl\">quality control</span> of a <span class=\"hl\">series</span> of 200 steel shafts. First, he takes a <span class=\"hl\">sample</span> from the <span class=\"hl\">batch</span>. Each shaft <span class=\"hl\">is measured</span> with a caliper and a micrometer, and every dimension is compared to the <span class=\"hl\">nominal</span> value on the drawing. A part that is <span class=\"hl\">out of tolerance</span> is a <span class=\"hl\">non-conforming</span> part, and it is put aside.",
    "So far, Théo <span class=\"hl\">has checked</span> fifty parts. Most of them are <span class=\"hl\">within</span> the limits, but two shafts are 0.03 mm <span class=\"hl\">larger than</span> the maximum size — they are <span class=\"hl\">too big</span>. He <span class=\"hl\">found</span> the same <span class=\"hl\">deviation</span> yesterday, so the <span class=\"hl\">reject rate</span> is higher than last week.",
    "The team leader <span class=\"hl\">said</span> that the whole batch <span class=\"hl\">had to be</span> inspected 100 %. Théo thinks the tool <span class=\"hl\">must be</span> worn, because the parts <span class=\"hl\">can't</span> all drift by chance. He has written a non-conformity report, and the series has been put on hold until the machine is checked. ✅"
  ],
